Sorry about the format of that first post. I didn't know
that cutting and pasting from Notepad would add in all those
carriage returns (that's sort of an obsolete term isn't
it?). I tested this in alt.test so I believe it will work
correctly this time. Also, please forgive any wrong gender
pronouns, it was confusing to write and I was still finding
a few when repairing the format.

This is the story of Elric and her dog/cockatrice/rock troll
Bandit. Let's start with Bandit, since she did, indeed,
start first. Bandit entered the dungeons with no doubts,
fully trusting her brave master, Loki the Footpad. That
trust was totally misplaced! Loki was the first of 14 rogues
to die horribly in the dungeons, and by far the most naive. 

Bandit managed to keep him alive for over 3000 turns, all
the way to a general store on DL4! There Bandit fetched many
items for Loki before Loki came up with the brilliant idea
of reading a spellbook and then selling it back. Alas, if
Loki had been smart he might have succeeded, but if he had
been smart he wouldn't have tried it. Loki was blinded. Loki
tried to wait it out, but got hungry and blundered into Ms.
Upernavik, you know the rest.

