What was Bandit to do but settle down there with Ms.
Upernavik. Bandit wasn't happy. Ms. Upernavik treated her
poorly and didn't feed her at all. Fifteen more rogues and
four priests came and went without anyone coming to rescue
Bandit. Once there was a great commotion in the general
direction of the upstairs and Bandit ran like the wind to
see what was happening but before she could get there,
silence descended again leaving Bandit to cope with Ms.
Upernavik.

Then Elric came. Elric got off to a faltering start.

Elric the Aspirant  St:12 Dx:12 Co:11 In:9 Wi:20 Ch:9
Chaotic
Dlvl:1  $:0  HP:13(13) Pw:7(7) AC:7  Exp:1 T:1

Homely and dumb for an elf. All the other priests had been
neutral with plans to eventually wield Mojo, but with Elric,
the name led to the race, which didn't fit the master plan
at all! On top of that, Elric had been taught that he should
let Sundance, his kitten, kill all the newts, grid bugs and
jackals so he would grow quickly and protect Elric. Sundance
was killed by the first jackal, barely 20 moves into the
game, sigh.

Elric wasn't excited about his starting spells, protection
and stone to flesh. Despite their mundane nature, they both
saved Elric's life on at least one occasion. On DL2 Elric
found a huge deli (11x5) and had the foresight to buy a
carrot and a eucalyptus leaf. The carrot was used to recover
sight before telepathy or a unihorn. The eucalyptus leaf was
used on the astral plane during a battle with Pestilence. On
DL3 there was another deli and Elric bought some tripe.

Meanwhile Bandit grew more and more angry over the months of
neglect and determined to take out her anger on the next
adventurer so foolish as to cross her path. While brooding
over her lot in life, Bandit heard yet another cacophony in
the direction of the stairs. This time Bandit arrived in
time to see a scrawny, ugly elf in a robe throwing tripe to
a large dog. There were dead rats everywhere and a brown
pudding still trying to slide over to the elf. Bandit made
for the elf with breakneck speed, determined to rip his
throat out.

Wait, what's this, a cookie, the other dog got tripe! Well,
maybe this cookie is good, Bandit decided, and suddenly she
took a liking to this homely elf named Elric. Life was good.
Bandit and her new friend Samwise were both large dogs and
took quite good care of their friend Elric. Elric, in turn,
made up meatballs from time to time, and always kept his
dogs near by making a beautiful noise with a blessed leaf.

Elric went to visit Ms. Upernavik and bought a blindfold and
spent quite a while getting quotes on various items. The
dogs couldn't steal most of the stuff because it was cursed
(Elric just seemed to know those things!) Then the troop
headed back for the mines. 

Elric was generous with his meatballs and the ranks grew to
6 pets at one point. In minetown Elric foolishly lost all
his gold and a red spellbook because he thought, as a
priest, he was wise enough to learn new spells. Thereafter
Elric vowed to only read blessed spellbooks until he was a
much more mature priest. The temple was cross-aligned.

Next goal was Sokoban but on DL6 there was a lawful altar
and another dog named Samwise. This new dog was tamed and
renamed Samwise, Sr. since he was older. There was a big
pile of stuff, mostly cursed and unusable. A /oCancel fixed
much of it. A blue jelly corpse netted poison resistance and
Elric was starting to feel hopeful, but still no MR or
reflection. The altar was converted and 2 c?oCM improved
luck substantially but nothing else.

Now, Sokoban. Bandit was proud to be the only dog allowed to
go with Elric into Sokoban and, at the top, a magical bag
was found and blessed, after Bandit killed about a hundred
monsters of course! Back to mine's end for the luckstone. No
excitement, no poly traps.

The next real adventure was DL12. It was just one huge room
with monsters coming from every direction. Elric burned
Elbereth into the floor and then helped his pets as much as
he could without leaving the safety of the stairs. Elric had
long since tossed away his mace and was using a silver spear
which was enchanted up to +3. Elric did sneak off his base
once to nab a wraith corpse and XL13.

The carnage was terrible, Samwise and Edgar were killed
outright, Spidey ate a doppleganger corpse and became a
giant rat leading to the inevitable. Bandit ate a chameleon
corpse and became a cockatrice. A succubus came late to the
party and helped Elric to XL14 but then she started messing
about with Bandit, got stoned and was of no further use!

Down through the dungeon, a cross-aligned temple was spotted
on DL15. On DL17 there was a small throne room with one
white dragon and a several really wimpy monsters. Elric used
his protection spell several times and then took on the
dragon with his silver spear. It was getting scary at 34/77
HP but the dragon fell to the next thrust. AND, IT LEFT
SCALES! 

The stashes were searched and the scales soon became WDSM!
Much better weight and AC! DL18 had a general store, which
was handy for figuring out enchantment on some of the
weapons Elric had collected. It was notable that Elric got
his very first lizard corpse on DL18 as a XL14 character.
There are disadvantages to having many pets.

This level also contained the portal to Ludios. Elric
cleared the first room but wisely retired to the main
dungeon, waiting for reflection before going further.

A lawful temple was on DL22 and on DL24 a titan stood guard
in the Medusa entry hall! A quick retreat was in order.
Since a [SoR had been found, the little army returned to
Ludios. The doors were opened and Elric waited near the
portal to deal with a few opponents at a time. Two retreats
for healing were needed and poor Smokey, the large cat, was
killed. Around back, a magic harp was used to tame Rocky and
Frosty, trolls of the type you might guess.

An extended sac session (21 c?oCM and 12 /oCM broken on the
last charge) back on DL15 got Elric gifted with Sting (first
artifact @ 42,000 turns) crowned and given Stormbringer and,
eventually given Trollsbane, Werebane and Orchrist. Thanks.
Demonbane was found in the dungeon. Those, the Mitre of
Holiness and the invocation artifacts were all the artifacts
in the game.

The quest was done with little of note, except maybe the sex
change accident with the unIDed amulet! On arrival in
Nalzok's den, Elric burned Elbereth into the upstairs and
waited with her trusty silver spear. Nalzok finally came and
it was no contest. Elric stopped eating wraiths at XL 21,
Frosty got three XLs and Bandit one.

The final tour of the upper dungeon was done and Bandit had
the pleasure 
of watching Rocky and Frosty exact her revenge on Ms.
Upernavik. That was pretty much the crew now, and they were
pretty much kept on for sentimental reasons. All spellbooks
were collected. Elric blessed each until she found Identify
and then only blessed a few.

Back on the Medusa level, the titan summoned a horde before
he could be put to sleep. As the battle raged a gremlin
started dividing on the south side of the entry hall. By the
time Elric could get things under control in the north there
must have been 50 of them and Rocky and Bandit were only
interested in eating the vanquished. A little patience was
in order but Elric lost her head and slaughtered the lot.
Now she was insufficiently chaotic for quite a while. Funny,
seemed to Elric 
that going berzerk and killing an army of gremlins was a
pretty chaotic thing to do.

In one of the mazes before the castle, an encounter with a
master mind flayer resulted in a tactic Elric used
throughout the rest of the game. Elric wore jumping boots
and was fast, except when she used her spell to be very
fast. She cast haste self, threw his +6 spears a the MMF,
jumped away when necessary and repeated. A point of INT came
along with that kill.

On the last level before the castle Frosty was lost again
but a poly trap and a magic whistle helped Bandit become a
rock troll which would have been more useful than a
cockatrice had Elric needed further assistance. Elric was
looking pretty buff by now:

