The castle was conquered and the VotD cleared. A massive
alchemy session got the HP up to 260 or so. Then the
decision had to be made on holding to a wishless conduct.
Genoless had been abandoned long ago when liches appeared
before MR. Polyless was still in play but with no MR, Elric
decided it was better to give up the conduct than lose the
game, so in rapid fire order (wand (0:1)) he wished up 2
b?oCharging, GDSM, and a magic marker (0:29) yuk! (but it
charged to (1:99)). Last minute wishes for speed boots and
another MM came just before meeting Rodney.

As Bandit and Elric left the maze just below the VotD,
Bandit got separated from Elric. Elric had really become
very inattentive with the pets and Bandit worried. What
seemed an eternity went by. Occasionally Bandit would sense
a magical surge that reminded her of Elric, but Elric never
was actually on the dungeon level. Bandit had almost given
up hope, but memories of all those delicious meatballs and
exciting adventures with Elric sustained her.

And then it happened! Elric was back, carrying some funny
looking amulet! Bandit was so happy! And Elric seemed
genuinely happy to see Bandit as well. She even had some of
her special meatballs! As they trekked up through the
dungeon, Elric told Bandit many stories of close calls and
narrow escapes. There was the time in the treasure zoo,
while wielding a cockatrice corpse, when the peaceful quasit
feel into the spiked pit, and the time the cockatrice hissed
at Elric while Elric was satiated, and the time a MMF was
summoned beside Elric while she was burdened. Bandit didn't
particularly like the cockatrice stories.

Elric complained about the difficulty of climbing out of
Gehennom, sharing her notes with Bandit, but Bandit didn't
understand:

